# Network Footprinting and Network Scanning

## Week 2 – Network Walks Internship Project

### Project Overview

This project was completed as part of the Week 2 internship activities at Network Walks. It focuses on two important cybersecurity concepts: Website Footprinting and Network Scanning.

The project demonstrates the use of Kali Linux tools for collecting publicly available website information and Zenmap for basic network host discovery.

## Project Modules

### Module 1: Website Footprinting

**Target Domain:** `networkwalks.com`

**Operating System:** Kali Linux

The following tools were used:

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| WHOIS | Collect domain registration information |
| WhatWeb | Identify website technologies |
| Nslookup | Retrieve DNS information |
| cURL | Examine HTTP response headers |
| WAFW00F | Detect Web Application Firewall |
| DNSRecon | Enumerate DNS records |

### Module 2: Network Scanning with Zenmap

**Operating System:** Windows

**Tool:** Zenmap (Nmap)

A Ping scan was performed to identify an active host using the target IP address from the practical session.

**Scan Configuration:**
- Scan Profile: Ping Scan
- Target: `192.168.56.1`
- Command: `nmap -sn 192.168.56.1`

**Scan Result:**
- IP addresses scanned: 1
- Live hosts identified: 1
- Scan duration: 1.25 seconds

## Objectives

- Understand the fundamentals of website footprinting.
- Collect publicly available domain information.
- Identify website technologies and DNS records.
- Examine HTTP response headers.
- Understand Web Application Firewall detection.
- Learn basic network scanning using Zenmap.
- Identify active hosts through Ping scanning.
- Document practical results and observations.

## Technologies and Tools Used

- Kali Linux
- Windows
- Oracle VirtualBox
- WHOIS
- WhatWeb
- Nslookup
- cURL
- WAFW00F
- DNSRecon
- Zenmap (Nmap)

